  "articleBody": "Facing a DUI charge in California can be really scary, and you might feel like there's no way out, especially with the strict laws here. But here's the thing: you absolutely can fight a DUI charge. It's not an automatic conviction, and there are many avenues an experienced criminal defense attorney can explore to challenge the allegations against you. For example, your attorney might question the legality of the traffic stop, the calibration and accuracy of breathalyzer tests, or the procedures used by law enforcement during your arrest. They can also examine whether field sobriety tests were administered correctly or if there were any medical conditions that could have influenced the results. Whether it's a first-time DUI, a repeat offense, or a felony charge, a skilled lawyer can work to get charges reduced, dismissed, or pursue alternative sentencing options like diversion programs. Getting professional help early on is critical to protecting your driving privileges and your future. Don't assume defeat; explore your options with someone who knows the system.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-26"
}